{"Multiple r.log.Error() calls are used for routine cleanup progress logging with messages like 'Annotations to clean by time' and 'cleaned annotations by time'. These are informational/debug messages, not errors. Using Error level will pollute error logs, potentially trigger monitoring alerts, and log potentially large amounts of data. The err parameter logged at lines 534, 554, and 576 is always nil at that point since errors are returned early above.": 0.9720873236656189, "The cleanup job ticker was changed from time.Minute * 10 to time.Minute * 1. This change isn't mentioned in the PR description which focuses solely on fixing MySQL deadlocks. Running cleanup 10x more frequently increases database load significantly and creates a mismatch with the 9-minute timeout defined on line 89, potentially causing overlapping cleanup operations.": 0.9418616890907288, "The deleteByIDs function builds the ID list string using repeated fmt.Sprintf('%s, %d', values, v) concatenation in a loop, which is O(n\u00b2) complexity due to creating a new string allocation on each iteration. For batch sizes up to 32767, this creates tens of thousands of intermediate strings. The same file already uses bytes.Buffer for SQL building elsewhere, which would be O(n) and more consistent with existing patterns.": 0.6328861713409424}